+ * its flips (every host bit is on two of its edges, and a cycle has an even number of edges). A
+ * cycle whose flips xor to 1 has at least one break and one suffices; a path or an even cycle can
+ * have none. So the floor is the number of odd cycles: a lower bound on those two rounds' part of any
+ * timetable's least.
